{"title":"Venkata Rohith Reddy Matli, Ph.D.","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Venkata Rohith Reddy Matli, Ph.D."},"headingText":"Hello!","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n<!-- Floating Assistant Container -->\n<div id=\"avatar-container\" class=\"floating-avatar\">\n  <div id=\"avatar-sprite\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<style>\n.floating-avatar {\n  position: fixed;\n  top: 140px;  /* Pushed down to clear the top navigation bar */\n  left: 30px;  \n  \n  width: 240px; \n  height: 240px; \n  \n  transform: scale(0.65);\n  transform-origin: top left; \n  \n  border-radius: 50%; \n  overflow: hidden;\n  z-index: 9999;\n  pointer-events: none; \n}\n\n#avatar-sprite {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  background-image: url('assets/motion.webp');\n  background-repeat: no-repeat;\n  background-position: 0px 0px; \n  mix-blend-mode: multiply; \n}\n</style>\n\n<script>\ndocument.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n  const avatarContainer = document.getElementById(\"avatar-container\");\n  const sprite = document.getElementById(\"avatar-sprite\");\n  \n  const CELL_WIDTH = 240;\n  const CELL_HEIGHT = 240;\n  const COLUMNS = 11;        \n  const TOTAL_FRAMES = 121;   \n  \n  let ticking = false;\n\n  window.addEventListener(\"scroll\", () => {\n    if (!ticking) {\n      window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n        const scrollPx = window.scrollY || document.documentElement.scrollTop;\n        \n        // ==========================================\n        // 1. THE ANIMATION FIX\n        // ==========================================\n        const maxPossibleScroll = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;\n        const SCROLL_THRESHOLD = Math.min(600, maxPossibleScroll); \n        \n        let scrollPercent = Math.min(scrollPx / SCROLL_THRESHOLD, 1.0);\n        let frameIndex = Math.floor(scrollPercent * (TOTAL_FRAMES - 1));\n        \n        const col = frameIndex % COLUMNS;\n        const row = Math.floor(frameIndex / COLUMNS);\n        const posX = -(col * CELL_WIDTH);\n        const posY = -(row * CELL_HEIGHT);\n        \n        sprite.style.backgroundPosition = `${posX}px ${posY}px`;\n        \n        // ==========================================\n        // 2. THE FADE-OUT EFFECT\n        // ==========================================\n        // Starts fading immediately, completely invisible by just 150px of scrolling!\n        const FADE_THRESHOLD = 150; \n        let opacity = 1 - (scrollPx / FADE_THRESHOLD);\n        avatarContainer.style.opacity = Math.max(opacity, 0);\n\n        ticking = false;\n      });\n      ticking = true;\n    }\n  });\n});\n</script>\n\n\n<!-- THE MAIN CONTENT (Centered with max-width) -->\n<div style=\"max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding-top: 20px;\">\n\n\nI am a Data Scientist and **applied researcher** with a **Ph.D. in Spatial Statistics**. Over the past eight years, I have built predictive models to make sense of everything from large-scale networks to complex environmental systems. \n\nMy true passion lies in taking highly complex spatial data and turning it into clear, rigorous insights. I enjoy blending foundational statistical methods, like **Bayesian inference** and **geostatistics**, with **modern AI tools** to build intelligent systems and novel methodologies that solve hard problems. \n\nRight now, my interests lie at the intersection of **AI Agentic Workflows** and **Complex Spatial Networks**. I am leveraging my background in computational statistics to explore how we can design AI systems capable of reasoning through and optimizing spatial data on their own.\n\n### Core Research & Technical Competencies\n* **Modelling & Statistics:** Geostatistics, Bayesian Inference, Spatiotemporal Analysis, XGBoost, Monte Carlo Simulation.\n* **Programming:** Python, R, SQL, SAS, Matlab.\n* **AI & Machine Learning:** Prompt Engineering, GenAI Integrations, Agentic Workflows.\n* **Data & Geospatial:** PostgreSQL, Amazon Redshift, ArcGIS/QGIS, Tableau.\n\n---\n\n**[Email](mailto:vrrmatli@gmail.com)** &nbsp;|&nbsp; **[LinkedIn](https://linkedin.com/in/vmatli)** &nbsp;|&nbsp; **[Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=SHjYPf8AAAAJ&hl=en&authuser=4)** &nbsp;|&nbsp; **[GitHub](https://github.com/vrrmatli)**\n\n</div>","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n<!-- Floating Assistant Container -->\n<div id=\"avatar-container\" class=\"floating-avatar\">\n  <div id=\"avatar-sprite\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<style>\n.floating-avatar {\n  position: fixed;\n  top: 140px;  /* Pushed down to clear the top navigation bar */\n  left: 30px;  \n  \n  width: 240px; \n  height: 240px; \n  \n  transform: scale(0.65);\n  transform-origin: top left; \n  \n  border-radius: 50%; \n  overflow: hidden;\n  z-index: 9999;\n  pointer-events: none; \n}\n\n#avatar-sprite {\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  background-image: url('assets/motion.webp');\n  background-repeat: no-repeat;\n  background-position: 0px 0px; \n  mix-blend-mode: multiply; \n}\n</style>\n\n<script>\ndocument.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n  const avatarContainer = document.getElementById(\"avatar-container\");\n  const sprite = document.getElementById(\"avatar-sprite\");\n  \n  const CELL_WIDTH = 240;\n  const CELL_HEIGHT = 240;\n  const COLUMNS = 11;        \n  const TOTAL_FRAMES = 121;   \n  \n  let ticking = false;\n\n  window.addEventListener(\"scroll\", () => {\n    if (!ticking) {\n      window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n        const scrollPx = window.scrollY || document.documentElement.scrollTop;\n        \n        // ==========================================\n        // 1. THE ANIMATION FIX\n        // ==========================================\n        const maxPossibleScroll = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;\n        const SCROLL_THRESHOLD = Math.min(600, maxPossibleScroll); \n        \n        let scrollPercent = Math.min(scrollPx / SCROLL_THRESHOLD, 1.0);\n        let frameIndex = Math.floor(scrollPercent * (TOTAL_FRAMES - 1));\n        \n        const col = frameIndex % COLUMNS;\n        const row = Math.floor(frameIndex / COLUMNS);\n        const posX = -(col * CELL_WIDTH);\n        const posY = -(row * CELL_HEIGHT);\n        \n        sprite.style.backgroundPosition = `${posX}px ${posY}px`;\n        \n        // ==========================================\n        // 2. THE FADE-OUT EFFECT\n        // ==========================================\n        // Starts fading immediately, completely invisible by just 150px of scrolling!\n        const FADE_THRESHOLD = 150; \n        let opacity = 1 - (scrollPx / FADE_THRESHOLD);\n        avatarContainer.style.opacity = Math.max(opacity, 0);\n\n        ticking = false;\n      });\n      ticking = true;\n    }\n  });\n});\n</script>\n\n\n<!-- THE MAIN CONTENT (Centered with max-width) -->\n<div style=\"max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding-top: 20px;\">\n\n## Hello!\n\nI am a Data Scientist and **applied researcher** with a **Ph.D. in Spatial Statistics**. Over the past eight years, I have built predictive models to make sense of everything from large-scale networks to complex environmental systems. \n\nMy true passion lies in taking highly complex spatial data and turning it into clear, rigorous insights. I enjoy blending foundational statistical methods, like **Bayesian inference** and **geostatistics**, with **modern AI tools** to build intelligent systems and novel methodologies that solve hard problems. \n\nRight now, my interests lie at the intersection of **AI Agentic Workflows** and **Complex Spatial Networks**. I am leveraging my background in computational statistics to explore how we can design AI systems capable of reasoning through and optimizing spatial data on their own.\n\n### Core Research & Technical Competencies\n* **Modelling & Statistics:** Geostatistics, Bayesian Inference, Spatiotemporal Analysis, XGBoost, Monte Carlo Simulation.\n* **Programming:** Python, R, SQL, SAS, Matlab.\n* **AI & Machine Learning:** Prompt Engineering, GenAI Integrations, Agentic Workflows.\n* **Data & Geospatial:** PostgreSQL, Amazon Redshift, ArcGIS/QGIS, Tableau.\n\n---\n\n**[Email](mailto:vrrmatli@gmail.com)** &nbsp;|&nbsp; **[LinkedIn](https://linkedin.com/in/vmatli)** &nbsp;|&nbsp; **[Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=SHjYPf8AAAAJ&hl=en&authuser=4)** &nbsp;|&nbsp; **[GitHub](https://github.com/vrrmatli)**\n\n</div>"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["styles.css"],"toc":true,"output-file":"index.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other 